    <item ident="g83edc8d4d84ca4e44e31446dc22ba183" title="Recursion">
      <itemmetadata>
        <qtimetadata>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>question_type</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>multiple_choice_question</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>points_possible</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>1.0</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>original_answer_ids</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>6271,3719,4174,1487</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
        </qtimetadata>
      </itemmetadata>
      <presentation>
        <material>
          <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;A developer is tasked with creating a function to calculate the total size of all files within a directory structure, represented by a nested JavaScript object. The structure can have folders nested within other folders to an unknown depth. Each file has a &lt;code&gt;size&lt;/code&gt; property, and each folder has a &lt;code&gt;children&lt;/code&gt; property containing more files or folders.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;const directory = {&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; name: 'root',&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; children: [&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; { name: 'file1.txt', size: 100 },&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; {&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; name: 'folderA',&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; children: [&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; { name: 'file2.txt', size: 250 },&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; {&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; name: 'subfolderB',&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; children: [{ name: 'file3.txt', size: 50 }]&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; }&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; ]&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; },&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; { name: 'file4.txt', size: 120 }&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; ]&lt;br&gt;};&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Which programming concept is best suited for elegantly solving this problem, where a function must navigate a data structure of unknown and variable depth?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</mattext>
        </material>
        <response_lid ident="response1" rcardinality="Single">
          <render_choice>
            <response_label ident="6271">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Recursion, where the function calls itself to calculate the size of sub-folders and adds it to the total.</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="3719">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">A single for...of loop to iterate through the top-level children array and sum the sizes.</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="4174">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">A  .map() function to create a new array containing only the file sizes.</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="1487">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">A while loop that continues as long as the total size is less than a predefined limit.</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
          </render_choice>
        </response_lid>
      </presentation>
      <resprocessing>
        <outcomes>
          <decvar maxvalue="100" minvalue="0" varname="SCORE" vartype="Decimal"/>
        </outcomes>
        <respcondition continue="No">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">6271</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <setvar action="Set" varname="SCORE">100</setvar>
        </respcondition>
      </resprocessing>
    </item>
    <item ident="g74306f8d19fac3ec30510fbdddeb6839" title="Template Element">
      <itemmetadata>
        <qtimetadata>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>question_type</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>multiple_choice_question</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>points_possible</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>1.0</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>original_answer_ids</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>8131,3131,4453,6909</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
        </qtimetadata>
      </itemmetadata>
      <presentation>
        <material>
          <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;What is a key🔑 characteristic of the HTML &lt;code data-start="155" data-end="167"&gt;&amp;lt;template&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; element?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</mattext>
        </material>
        <response_lid ident="response1" rcardinality="Single">
          <render_choice>
            <response_label ident="8131">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">It holds HTML content that is not rendered until it is activated via JavaScript.</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="3131">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">It renders its content immediately when the page loads.</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="4453">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">It allows CSS to be scoped to a specific element.</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="6909">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">It is required for all form elements to function correctly.</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
          </render_choice>
        </response_lid>
      </presentation>
      <resprocessing>
        <outcomes>
          <decvar maxvalue="100" minvalue="0" varname="SCORE" vartype="Decimal"/>
        </outcomes>
        <respcondition continue="No">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">8131</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <setvar action="Set" varname="SCORE">100</setvar>
        </respcondition>
      </resprocessing>
    </item>
